- DONE (2026-08-10) Make it so that every OCPQ generated file gets deleted after it is created during the evaluation.
  Result files are discarded once the metric has read them (`keep_result_files: true` to retain);
  generated query JSONs are kept deliberately as the raw-output audit trail (CLAUDE.md 2.3).
  Investigating this found a bigger problem: results were recovered by globbing a directory shared
  by all 24 concurrent array tasks, so a task could silently read another task's result — measured
  at 4/12 wrong results under concurrency. Each invocation now runs in its own scratch directory.
  See Thesis/notes/11-evaluation-readiness.md 6.3.
- DONE Since the root node's bindings aren't the only thing required for the results, how do I compare two queries that do the same thing but have different nodes?
  Answered as Q11 and implemented: only the root binding box is compared, located via
  `root_node_index()` rather than assumed to be index 0, with each situation keyed as
  (event indices, object indices, violated). Invariant to variable numbering and node count.
  See Thesis/notes/08-metric-defect.md.
- DONE (2026-08-10) Save the query combinations that were too different (result-wise) between the LLM and the gold query during the evaluation. Make sure it is not taking too much space. It should be mainly used to see what weaknesses/mess-ups the LLM does.
  `analyze_divergence.py` writes divergence_report.json into every run dir and merged output.
  No new data is captured - predictions.json already holds everything (~40 MB for the full
  matrix), so the report is a view over it, capped at 3 examples per (class x condition).
  Classes: schema_invalid / execution_failed / empty_result / wrong_population / over_selection /
  under_selection / partial. `bb_dropped` names the building blocks the model failed to express.
  Also fixed: failure_log.jsonl now lands in the run dir (24 array tasks shared one path before),
  a crash in slice_results_by_bb._mean on any non-executing prediction, and the analysis steps are
  now guarded so they cannot fail a completed run. See Thesis/notes/11-evaluation-readiness.md 6.4.
- Give field types (e.g., string, bool, float) to the LLM during the prompting and explicitly ask it to cast variables that need to if using CEL. 